 ## Background
-The Gradient Descent Solver, particularly the Adam optimizer variant, was introduced by Kingma and Ba in 2015 [S2, unofficial][S3]. It has been widely adopted in differentiable volume rendering and inverse problems due to its ability to handle stochastic gradients and adapt learning rates per parameter [S2, unofficial][S3]. In the context of volume rendering, it is used to optimize voxel grid parameters and transfer functions [S1, S2, unofficial].
+The Gradient Descent Solver, particularly the Adam optimizer variant, was introduced by Kingma and Ba in 2015 [S2, unofficial][S3]. It updates voxel grid parameters in differentiable volume rendering [S2, unofficial] and addresses gradient noise and anisotropy by filtering gradients temporally [S3]. In volume rendering, it optimizes transfer functions [S1, unofficial] and voxel grid parameters [S2, unofficial].
 
